AFFIDAVIT

I, Dr. Suresh Chandra Purohit, S/o Late Shri Rameshwar Purohit, aged 58 years,
residing at 5, Sardarpura, Jodhpur – 342 005,
Dam Engineering Consultant,
do hereby solemnly affirm and state as follows:

1. I am a qualified Dam Engineer with 32 years of experience in irrigation and dam projects
   and have been engaged as a consultant by M/s. Jal Nirman Constructions Ltd. for the
   Sukli Medium Irrigation Dam Project.

2. I have personally inspected the construction site on multiple occasions and have
   reviewed all technical drawings, geological reports, and quality compliance records.

3. Regarding the geological surprise: I have reviewed the initial geo-technical report
   provided by WRD (dated July 2019) which indicated Type I soft rock. I have also
   reviewed the WRD Site Visit Report dated 15.01.2020 which confirmed Type III hard rock.

4. This discrepancy is a clear case of geological surprise as per CPWD GCC Clause 12
   and FIDIC Sub-Clause 4.12. The contractor could not have reasonably anticipated
   Type III rock based on the initial report.

5. The additional cost of ₹4.82 Crore for drilling, blasting, and heavy machinery is
   reasonable and justified based on my assessment of the rock hardness and required
   construction methods.

6. Regarding the design revision: The spillway capacity increase from 1200 cumecs to
   1500 cumecs is a valid engineering decision by WRD for safety enhancement,
   considering updated flood routing studies.

7. The additional work due to revised spillway design should be compensated as per
   CPWD GCC Clause 12 (Variations). The rate analysis prepared by my office shows
   that the fair compensation for this additional work is ₹3.87 Crore.

8. Regarding quality of work: I have personally inspected all concrete work in the dam
   wall, foundation, and spillway structure. The quality is fully compliant with:
   - IS 456:2000 (Plain and Reinforced Concrete Code)
   - IS 11294:1985 (Criteria for Structural Safety of Dams)
   - Central Water Commission (CWC) Guidelines for Dam Construction

9. Test certificates for all concrete cubes (cylinder tests) show 100% compliance with
   target strength of M-35 grade. No structural deficiencies have been identified.

10. Regarding the cofferdam breach: The rainfall of 450mm in 24 hours on 12.06.2021 is
    indeed unprecedented for the region. As per meteorological records, the highest
    recorded 24-hour rainfall in the area was 280mm (1965). This qualifies as an Act
    of God event under Force Majeure.

11. The cost of ₹3.20 Crore for cofferdam reconstruction, de-silting, and foundation
    repair is reasonable based on standard rates for dam construction.

12. All facts stated above are within my professional knowledge and are true to the best of my
    information and belief. No part of it is false and nothing material has been concealed.

Deponent: Dr. Suresh Chandra Purohit
Date: 15.10.2022
Place: Jodhpur

Sworn before me:
